From 144d07a850cd754a34118dad382b12ebbc02e467 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Britten <11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:59:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat: open a project read-only with --read-only and
 open_project read_only

camcraft-ui --read-only job.camproj opens a project read-only. The MCP
tool open_project takes read_only: true for the same result.

- One rule, project::refuse_read_only_save, refuses a save to the file
  that the project is open read-only from. The window's save and
  script::api::v_save call it, so MCP save_project, script cam.save and
  the live seam of a window are refused too. The file stays byte for
  byte.
- The rule compares canonical paths, so a save from the Save As dialog
  to the opened file is refused.
- In the window, Save on a read-only project opens the Save As dialog.
  Save As to another file works and ends read-only.
- Changes stay allowed in memory. The title bar shows "(read-only)".
- A model file with --read-only is imported as usual. The live seam
  still refuses open_project.

No change to the file format or PROJECT_VERSION.

Decisions: docs/decisions/3609-read-only-open.md.

Fixes #3609

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
